  .cat-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* Every photograph is the same 360x236 frame, so nothing here has to line
     the fourteen up — they already are. The two bar meters are narrower than
     the frame and sit centred inside it, which the renderer does rather than
     the stylesheet: the letterboxing is invisible because the frame and the
     module share a background.

     Captured at three device pixels per logical one. Two put them at exactly
     1:1 on a retina display, which is no headroom — one notch of browser zoom
     and hairlines and six-pixel labels are being upscaled. */
  /* The mat around the picture. A meter photographed to the edge of its cell
     reads as a screenshot that has been cropped too tight; the space is what
     makes it a plate. It also fixes the displayed width, which the renderer is
     tuned to — see FRAME_W in scripts/render-modules.mjs. */
  .cat-shot {
