  /* `height: auto` is load-bearing, and its absence is invisible in the markup.
     Every picture here carries `width` and `height` attributes so its box has a
     shape before the file arrives — and those attributes are a definite height,
     which is enough to make `aspect-ratio` do nothing at all. The first version
     of this asked for a 4:3 box and got 550x862 instead: the plate stood twice
     as tall as the photograph inside it, with the picture floating in the middle
     of a field of panel. Letting the height follow the width is also the better
