  }

  .flow-name {
    margin-top: var(--s24);
  }

  .flow-body {
    margin-top: var(--s12);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  /* The connector.

     Borrowed rather than invented: the plugin's own panel draws the link
     between the host and the app as a dashed line running out of its mark, and
     that panel is the first plate in this row. The page is repeating the
     product's drawing, which is the only reason it is allowed to be teal — the
     signal hue means a measurement on this site and nothing else, and what
     travels this line is measurements.

     Hung from the plate rather than from the step, so it sits on the middle of
     the picture whatever the heading above it does. It is static: the site has
     no ambient motion anywhere, an animated dash needs either a gradient or an
     SVG and the first is against the house rules, and the arrow already says
     which way the audio is going. */
  .flow-step + .flow-step .flow-plate::before,
  .flow-step + .flow-step .flow-plate::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    /* An absolutely positioned box is placed against its container's *padding*
       box, which is inside the border — so plain `right: 100%` starts the line
       a hairline in. The line leaves the plate behind it and stops short of the
